/* book exam traps: An ASIC is not the same as full-custom. Most ASICs are standard-cell designs; full-custom is one style among several. | A masked gate array is not an FPGA. The gate array is wired by metal masks at the foundry and cannot change afterwards; the FPGA is configured by the user. | Standard cells share one height, not one width. The width changes with the function and the drive strength. | Break-even volume is the difference in NRE divided by the difference in unit cost. NRE divided by a single unit cost means nothing. | The lowest total cost is not the whole answer. Time to market and the cost of a respin can rule out the cheapest style. */
